;; Reviewed 2026-10-09 (written by Claude, from the design, the MACRO
;; manual and the debugger runs; for the user's review). Why this is
;; right:
;; - A pointer is a longword (section 14, item 3), .BLKL, and NIL is 0:
;;   list := NIL is CLRL, n # NIL is TSTL. It is the address of the
;;   block's data; the block's tag, its descriptor's address or 0, is the
;;   longword before.
;; - Every dereference, written (n^.value) or implied by a field or an
;;   index, moves the pointer to a register, which sets the condition
;;   codes, and traps when it is 0: code 4 at the designator's line and
;;   column (run-nil-trap, 50:38). it.link.key checks both pointers: MOVL
;;   4(R0), R0 sets the codes for the second BNEQ.
;; - NodeDesc's descriptor: its size, 8 (value at 0, next at 4),
;;   extension level 0, one pointer, at 4, and its own address as its
;;   base type at level 0. Push's NEW(p) passes 8 and its address to
;;   POC_NEW, CALLG with a list of 3 longwords in the frame, and stores
;;   R0 in p; head, a VAR parameter, is @4(AP).
;; - NEW of an open array checks each length, kept in the frame, to be
;;   positive, else trap 7 at NEW's position (run-new-trap, 51:23). The
;;   size is the product of the lengths and the element's size, plus the
;;   header, a longword per dimension: t's 6 + 4; g's 3 * 4 by EMUL, then
;;   * 2, then + 8, each step checked (EMUL's high longword 0 and its low
;;   one not negative, ADDL2's V bit) so that a block of 2 GB or more
;;   traps 7 too. The tag is 0: CHAR and INTEGER hold no pointers. When
;;   POC_NEW returns a block, the lengths are stored in its header.
;; - t's data is 4(R0) and its length (R0); g's lengths are (R0) and
;;   4(R0), its data 8(R0). An index is checked against its length, CMPL
;;   unsigned and BLSSU, else trap 2; g's row i is i times the second
;;   length times 2, MOVAB 8(R0)[R1], and j indexes it as a word, (R1)
;;   [R2]. COPY("hello", t^) and COPY(t^, word) are section 14 item 1's
;;   copy, limited by LEN(t^) - 1 and by 7, read from the header.
;; - NEW(r), an ARRAY 4 OF INTEGER, passes 8 and the tag 0; r[3] is
;;   6(R0).
;; - NEW(it.link), of VaxPtrLib's Item, names VaxPtrLib's descriptor,
;;   G^VAXPTRLIB_ITEMDESC_86IN7EB7, .EXTERNAL. it.link is located first,
;;   its base in R2, which POC_NEW's entry mask saves.
;; - The initializer's mask saves R2-R5, for MOVC3, LOCC, and g[2, 3]
;;   + g^[1][2]'s R2-R4.
;; - run-values examines what it computes, and three tags, which the
;;   debugger names: NodeDesc's descriptor for the list's first block,
;;   VaxPtrLib's ItemDesc's for it and for it.link.
; VaxPointers, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
